      "text": "Momentum is computed as the average of the two high-prior-return portfolios minus the average of the two low-prior-return portfolios: Mom = \u00bd(Small High + Big High) \u2212 \u00bd(Small Low + Big Low). The script reads only the first block of the file, the value-weighted monthly returns, and stops at the first blank or non-data line after it. It drops any month with a missing value (-99.99 or -999). I have not run it against the full file.\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\nrows = []\nstarted = False\nwith open(\"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_12_2.csv\") as f:\n    for line in f:\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.strip().split(\",\")]\n        is_data = len(parts) >= 7 and len(parts[0]) == 6 and parts[0].isdigit()\n        if is_data:\n            started = True\n            rows.append(parts[:7])\n        elif started:\n            break\n\ndf = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=[\"date\", \"sl\", \"sm\", \"sh\", \"bl\", \"bm\", \"bh\"])\ndf[\"date\"] = df[\"date\"].astype(int)\nfor c in [\"sl\", \"sm\", \"sh\", \"bl\", \"bm\", \"bh\"]:\n    df[c] = pd.to_numeric(df[c], errors=\"coerce\")\n    df.loc[df[c] <= -99.0, c] = np.nan\ndf = df.dropna()\ndf[\"value\"] = (df[\"sh\"] + df[\"bh\"]) / 2 - (df[\"sl\"] + df[\"bl\"]) / 2\ndf[[\"date\", \"value\"]].round(4).to_csv(\"output.csv\", index=False)\n```",
